# core-graph .trivyignore — applies to docker-scan job in .github/workflows/security.yml
#
# CVE-2025-68121
#   crypto/tls: Incorrect certificate validation during TLS session resumption.
#   Reported against /usr/local/bin/gosu (Go stdlib v1.24.0) inherited from
#   apache/age:release_PG16_1.6.0. gosu is a setuid helper used by the postgres
#   entrypoint; it does not exercise crypto/tls anywhere in its code path, so
#   the vulnerable bytes bundled into the static binary are unreachable at
#   runtime. apt-get dist-upgrade cannot fix this because gosu is shipped as a
#   downloaded binary, not via apt.
#
#   Latest upstream gosu release (1.19, 2025-09-23) is built with Go 1.24.6,
#   still below the Go 1.24.13 fix line. No upstream binary update available.
#   Drop this entry once tianon/gosu publishes a release built against
#   Go 1.24.13+ and Dockerfile.postgres is rebuilt to pick it up.
CVE-2025-68121
